config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_OWRTWIFI2DOMO
	bool "Domoticz plugin: presence detection from an OpenWrt router (owrtwifi2domo)"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	default n
	help
		presence detection driven by the WiFi clients associated to an OpenWrt router (it ships its own MQTT client and needs no additional Python module).

		It is a Python plugin of Domoticz: the package installs it into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/owrtwifi2domo, the directory Domoticz is
		started with (-approot of the domoticz package), and it needs no
		change of the Domoticz build.

		Setup -> Hardware -> owrtwifi2domo, enter the address and the credentials of the OpenWrt router.

		Licensed upstream (LICENSE is installed with the plugin). The
		repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a pinned commit of
		the default branch.
